@asbjornsabo For the naming, I've introduce a new struct `bt_csis_client_set_info` and renamed the `bt_csis_client_set` to `bt_csis_client_csis_inst`. 

I've also merge the two discovery functions. 

All the changes have been done in newly added commits to this PR.

@rymanluk @asbjornsabo  The only remaining part of this PR is now whether or not to keep the `bt_csis_client_get_lock_state` function, which implements one of the procedures in the CSIP spec, and is used by CAP. 

The lock state is read during discovery and we subscribe to notifications, so there's no need for the application to use it (unless notifications go missing). 

Personally I am in favor of keep the function, and then let the upper layers decide whether to use it or not.
